{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Your throne</b> — Some say: like 'You shall not curse Elohim' [i.e., the word is in construct]. The Gaon [Saadia] said: 'Your throne Elohim will establish.' In my opinion: the word כסאך functions for something else, in the manner of 'and the prophecy of Oded the prophet' [2 Chronicles 15:8], which is like 'and the prophecy, [namely] the prophecy of Oded the prophet.' So too here: 'Your throne, the throne of Elohim,' like 'and Solomon sat on the throne of YHWH' [1 Chronicles 29:23]. And one who says that כסאך means 'before HaShem' — the verse that comes after it will contradict him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:53.538968678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}